  "description": "Captures a family's whole existence as hauling water uphill. On a barren Seto Inland Sea island with no fresh water, parents row to the mainland and carry buckets up the slope, plant by plant, in near-total silence. Endurance, yes — but filmed as choreography, not punishment; it plays like a folk song about labour.\n\nA family of four are the sole inhabitants of a small island where they struggle each day to irrigate their crops.",
